Calculate the arc length of the sector shown, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (0:2.5);
\coordinate (B) at (80:2.5);
\draw (O) -- (A) node[midway,below] {$9\text{ m}$};
\draw (O) -- (B);
\draw (A) arc[start angle=0,end angle=80,radius=2.5];
\pic[draw,"$80^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.6cm,angle eccentricity=2] {angle=A--O--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Calculate the arc length of the sector shown, in exact form in terms of $\pi$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (0:2.5);
\coordinate (B) at (45:2.5);
\draw (O) -- (A) node[midway,below] {$16\text{ cm}$};
\draw (O) -- (B);
\draw (A) arc[start angle=0,end angle=45,radius=2.5];
\pic[draw,"$45^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.6cm,angle eccentricity=2.7] {angle=A--O--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The angle marked is the **exterior** angle of the sector. Calculate the arc length, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (0:2.5);
\coordinate (B) at (120:2.5);
\draw (O) -- (A) node[midway,below] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\draw (O) -- (B);
\draw (120:2.5) arc[start angle=120,end angle=360,radius=2.5];
\pic[draw,"$120^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.65cm,angle eccentricity=2.1] {angle=A--O--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Calculate the perimeter of the sector shown, correct to $1$ decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (0:2.5);
\coordinate (B) at (135:2.5);
\draw (O) -- (A) node[midway,below] {$4\text{ m}$};
\draw (O) -- (B);
\draw (A) arc[start angle=0,end angle=135,radius=2.5];
\pic[draw,"$135^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.6cm,angle eccentricity=2] {angle=A--O--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Calculate the perimeter of this quadrant, correct to $1$ decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\draw (O) -- (2.6,0) node[midway,below] {$7\text{ cm}$};
\draw (O) -- (0,2.6);
\draw (2.6,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=90,radius=2.6];
\draw (0.32,0) -- (0.32,0.32) -- (0,0.32);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Calculate the perimeter of this semicircle, in exact form in terms of $\pi$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\draw (-2.4,0) -- (2.4,0);
\draw (2.4,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=180,radius=2.4];
\fill (0,0) circle (1.6pt);
\draw[<->] (0,-0.5) -- (2.4,-0.5) node[midway,below] {$9\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Which expression gives the **perimeter** of the sector shown?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (0:2.5);
\coordinate (B) at (110:2.5);
\draw (O) -- (A) node[midway,below] {$r$};
\draw (O) -- (B) node[midway,above left] {$r$};
\draw (A) arc[start angle=0,end angle=110,radius=2.5];
\pic[draw,"$\theta$",angle radius=0.65cm,angle eccentricity=1.9] {angle=A--O--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The perimeter of this sector is $22$ m. Find the angle $\theta$ at the centre, correct to $1$ decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (0:2.4);
\coordinate (B) at (138:2.4);
\draw (O) -- (A) node[midway,below] {$5\text{ m}$};
\draw (O) -- (B);
\pic[draw,"$\theta$",angle radius=0.7cm,angle eccentricity=1.8] {angle=A--O--B};
\draw (A) arc[start angle=0,end angle=138,radius=2.4];
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
